From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 07:59:57 -0400
Subject: feat: clean links on every page opened (S-89)

A page the user opens now loads without the tracking parameters a
copied link loses, and a known redirect page that carries its target
in its own address is skipped to that target
(docs/features/clean-links.md Cl1-Cl3). CleanLinksThrottle, made in
ChromeContentBrowserClient::CreateURLLoaderThrottles, rewrites the
first address of a top-level GET in WillStartRequest, so the loader
makes an internal redirect before anything is sent. Subresources,
frames, POSTs, forms, reloads, restores, back and forward, and every
server redirect are left alone (Cl4, Cl5). HistoryTabHelper leaves
Stedding's own hop out of the redirect chain (Cl6). A Privacy row, on
by default, with a command-bar row (Cl7), and a list of kept sites in
Settings (Cl8, Cl9). Private windows clean too (Cl10). Nothing is
fetched (Cl11). Copy-link's table is shared and unchanged (Cl2,
copy-link L2). The copy-link and defaults browser tests turn the
setting off, since they test the copy and the address row, not this.

Why: tracking parameters reached the site on every link the user
opened; only a copied link was cleaned (BACKLOG S-89).
Removable when: never; the throttle and the history hunk go if
Chromium ships its own top-level parameter filter that does the same.
